{
  "about": "Real logos, each with its names, source page and licence. kind: game (the game tag, game switch, game boards and intro, matched on the plan's game), company, platform or brand (an in-game brand: its game lists the games it appears in, GTA VI only where official material shows it; the pictures are the GTA V versions), none = an outlet for the sourced-claim chip (caption5). Outlet logos for the sourced-claim animations (caption5) and game logos for the game tag (gametag). build_video.mjs puts an outlet logo in the source chip when the plan names that outlet, and a game logo in the game tag when the plan names that game, if its file is here. Images: transparent PNG, about 1280 px wide; they come with the Algrow download, like the footage. logo_h is the logo height in the chip (about 38 for a wordmark, 30 for a very long one, 61 for a square mark); logo_trim is 14 for a square mark, else 0. A game logo has no logo_h: the template sets its width. Its cx is its visual centre in logo widths from the image's centre (+ = right; the alpha-weighted centroid), so a year or a line under it centres on the artwork, not on the box; its door is [x, y, r] in logo widths from the centre: the middle and radius of its largest solid disc, where intro-B dives through it.",
